Instructions for complete installation of SWASH
-----------------------------------------------

Installation of SWASH can be done by means of the make and perl
utilities. Please carry out the following tasks:

   1) Ensure that the Perl package is available on your computer.
      Check it by typing 'perl -v'. The Perl version should be at
      least 5.0.0 or higher.

   2) Type 'make config' to create configuration file.
      This file (macros.inc) contains machine-dependent macros
      to be needed by the Makefile.

   3) Compilation of the SWASH source code for sequential runs can
      be done by typing 'make ser'. For parallel runs, linking the
      MPI libraries can be done by typing 'make mpi'.
      NOTE: This command must be preceded once by 'make config'.

   4) For more information, please consult the Implementation Manual ...

   5) ... or visit https://delftwaves.github.io/swash-docs/getting_started/install.html
